From 199f43aa46b580f6d340016d9da8fc4e3d64b306 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:26:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 45/45] wifi: xradio: XR829: connect and pass traffic

Port the remaining HT40 API (XR829 firmware) differences needed for
station mode, converting from the XR819 structures at the firmware
boundary so both chips keep sharing the driver:
- join/start: 16-bit PHY mode word (modem, width, band, preamble) at 20 MHz
- TX: rate retry policies as up to 6 rate entries (same 12 bytes), TX
  request header in the new layout (policy index, first rate entry,
  data offset, PTA priority), built from the XR819 one
- TX confirm: rate entry and per-rate tries translated back to rate indices
- association mode MIB: 12-byte layout with PHY mode word, renumbered flags
- ARP reply template: 8-byte header
- override internal TX rate MIB: two rate entries

WPA2 (CCMP) station mode works: 29 Mbit/s RX and 12 Mbit/s TX in iperf3
at MCS 7, stable over 2 minutes.

Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
